# Deleting a draft (`dossiers.md`, "Sent et Drafts"): a draft is not moved,
# only deleted. In Drafts, `d` (archive) is refused and says so; Delete
# puts the draft in Deleted, alone: the conversation it answers stays in
# the Inbox. `z` brings it back. (The fake mail has 7 conversations in
# Drafts; the reply's conversation keeps the subject of the mail answered.)
expect folder = Inbox
expect selected_subject ~ La facture de mars
key r
expect composing = true
type Brouillon à jeter
key esc
expect composing = false
expect flash ~ Reply kept in Drafts
key ;
key r
expect folder = Drafts
expect thread_count = 8
expect selected_subject ~ La facture de mars
key d
expect flash ~ A draft is not moved: Delete puts it in Deleted
expect thread_count = 8
key del
expect thread_count = 7
key z
expect thread_count = 8
# `z` does not put the cursor back on what it restores: Drafts opened
# again, the draft is the first row.
key ;
key i
key ;
key r
expect selected_subject ~ La facture de mars
key del
expect thread_count = 7
# The conversation answered is still in the Inbox.
key ;
key i
expect folder = Inbox
expect selected_subject ~ La facture de mars
# The draft is in Deleted: one conversation more than the 12 of the fake
# mail, the draft's.
key ;
key d
expect folder = Deleted
expect thread_count = 13
snap deleted
